<div class="phead"><div class="w"><ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="{{ PathBase }}/">Gablefen Realty</a></li><li>About</li></ol><p class="kick">The firm</p><h1>A window on Courthouse Square since 1978</h1><p class="lede">Gablefen Realty is a fictional independent brokerage in a fictional mill town. It is here as a worked example of a real estate website built on Raytha, a self-hosted, open-source .NET CMS.</p></div></div><section class="sec tight"><div class="w"><div class="dg"><div class="prose"><p>The office sits in a bay window at 12 Courthouse Square, in a room that used to belong to a cloth merchant. Ed Ellison opened the firm in 1978. His daughter Rowan runs it now, with four other agents and a plat book that still comes off the shelf.</p><p>The public site is the listing window, the town plat, the open-house board and the sold book. Behind sign-in, buyer clients have a desk for tours and shortlist notes, and agents have a deal board with private remarks. Both use Raytha's own user accounts and groups, so a private remark is never sent to a browser that should not see it.</p><p>The town, the people, the houses and the figures are invented and labeled as such. Phone numbers use the 555 range. There are no offer, payment or sign-up forms; in the story, the office opens accounts and writes offers on paper or by email.</p><h2>The office</h2><p>12 Courthouse Square, Gablefen (fictional). Weekdays 9:00 am to 5:00 pm. On market Saturdays, April through October, there is a table on the west side of the courthouse lawn from 8:00 am to noon.</p><p>(555) 014-1860 · hello@gablefen.example</p></div><aside class="card side"><p class="kick">On this site</p><p>16 homes, 5 neighborhoods, 5 agents, weekly open houses, house styles, a town plat, public market notes, and two members-only desks. Built on a fresh Raytha instance, with no client-side app in the layout.</p></aside></div></div></section>
